   "text": {
    "L1": "Every magnet has two poles: north and south. The pull is strongest at the poles, near the two ends.",
    "L2": "Attraction alone does not prove that an object is a magnet. Iron can be attracted too.",
    "L3": "Bring unlike poles together, such as north and south. They attract each other.",
    "L4": "Bring like poles together, such as north and north. They repel each other.",
    "L5": "Repulsion is the sure test for a magnet. If an object pushes away a pole of a known magnet, it is a magnet.",
    "L6": "If a magnet breaks, each piece becomes a complete magnet with its own north and south pole.",
    "L7": "So remember: unlike poles attract, like poles repel, and poles come in pairs."
   },
